            <div xml:id="d166">

                <pb facs="0138" n="129" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg129"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/913: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-16">June 16,
                        1940</date>.<lb/>[Received June 17—1 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>683. Embassy recommends that future purchases of transportation for Americans
                    being repatriated from Soviet Union and Soviet occupied Poland include rail
                    transportation from place of residence in Soviet Union, or from Lwow if evacuee
                    resident in Soviet occupied Poland, to Vladivostok and rail steamer
                    transportation thence to United States west coast port via Japan. Transportation
                    should be prepaid in United States if possible.</p>
                <p>[Here follow details as to services and costs.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
